From 0c6927adc646100ef90e3c2fa2c3d0e827311657 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hitori-chan
Subject: [PATCH] output: an overlay plane above the primary

COutputState::setOverlayBuffer() puts a whole-output buffer at 1:1 on
the CRTC's first overlay plane that takes ARGB8888, above the primary
(null turns it off); IOutput::hasOverlayPlane() and getOverlayFormats()
say whether there is one. The overlay goes into the atomic request only
when its buffer is committed or at a modeset: left out, the kernel and
DCP keep it as it is, so a buffer placed on the primary under it flips
alone. Its FB is pinned and presented as the cursor's, restated with
the primary's, released with the connector's, and refused by the legacy
and Wayland backends and through the multi-GPU blit.

On appledrm (an M3 Max, r217) the layout this drives, NV12 placed on
the primary under a full-screen AR24 overlay, takes TEST_ONLY and the
commit, 21,600 primary-only flips at 30 Hz kept the overlay with none
failed, and it drew +0.04 to +0.06 W over the primary alone.
